<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>JouleLab</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@300;400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('nav') %>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow mono">ENERGY BUDGET ESTIMATOR</p>
      <h1>Every joule.<br><em>Accounted for.</em></h1>
      <p class="sub">See what your firmware costs.<br>Build devices that live longer.</p>
      <div class="cta"><a class="run" href="#lab">Run simulation <span class="circ">↗</span></a><a class="wsl mono" href="/workspace">Open workspace ↗</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art">
      <p class="mono tag">THE ENERGY LAB<br><span>Hardware, made visible.</span></p>
      <div class="ring r1"></div><div class="ring r2"></div>
      <div class="tilt" id="tilt"><div class="stage" id="stage">
        <div class="layer l1" data-l="1"></div>
        <div class="layer l2" data-l="2"></div>
        <div class="layer l3" data-l="3"><i class="chip mono">ESP32<br><small>WROOM-32</small></i><i class="usb"></i><i class="pins pl"></i><i class="pins pr"></i><i class="btn b1"></i><i class="btn b2"></i><i class="led"></i><span class="mono lbl">JL / 032 &nbsp; JOULELAB / MEASURE · UNDERSTAND · OPTIMIZE</span></div>
        <div class="layer l4" data-l="4"><i class="ant"></i></div>
        <div class="layer l5 glass" data-l="5"><span class="mono">POWER PROFILING</span><b id="volt">3.30<small>V</small></b><em class="mono" id="amp">I 3.53 mA</em>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 200 50"><polyline points="0,40 40,40 40,30 70,30 70,18 100,18 100,28 130,28 130,10 200,10" fill="none" stroke="#1a6b5f" stroke-width="2"/></svg></div>
      </div></div>
      <ul class="legend" id="legend">
        <li data-l="5" tabindex="0"><span class="mono">L5 · MEASURE</span><b>Profiling overlay</b><small>Live supply readout: bus voltage and current from the INA219.</small></li>
        <li data-l="4" tabindex="0"><span class="mono">L4 · RADIO</span><b>Wi-Fi / BLE transmit</b><small>Wi-Fi 802.11 b/g/n and Bluetooth 4.2 + BLE. Transmit peaks near 183 mA, the largest cost in each cycle.</small></li>
        <li data-l="3" tabindex="0"><span class="mono">L3 · MCU</span><b>ESP32 core</b><small>ESP32-WROOM-32: dual-core Xtensa LX6 at up to 240 MHz, 520 KB SRAM, 4 MB flash, 34 GPIO. Active for milliseconds, then deep sleep at about 10 µA.</small></li>
        <li data-l="2" tabindex="0"><span class="mono">L2 · POWER</span><b>3.3 V rail</b><small>Regulator and copper traces feeding every firmware phase.</small></li>
        <li data-l="1" tabindex="0"><span class="mono">L1 · BASE</span><b>Substrate</b><small>Ground reference and mounting plane.</small></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mono cap">Illustrative hardware model</p>
      <button class="mono explode" id="explode" aria-expanded="false"><b id="exlabel">Explode layers</b> <span>+</span></button>
    </div>
    <div class="strip mono"><span>BUILT FOR EMBEDDED DEVELOPERS</span><span>ESP32 &nbsp;•&nbsp; STM32 &nbsp;•&nbsp; BLACK PILL</span></div>
  </section>

  <div id="root"></div>

  <section class="esp" id="esp32">
    <div>
      <p class="mono small">ESP32 · DETAILED PROFILE</p>
      <h2>The chip behind<br>the numbers.</h2>
      <p class="lead">The ESP32 model uses datasheet-typical figures. Real boards vary with module revision, supply, firmware and antenna, so validate by measurement.</p>
      <dl class="spec">
        <% esp32.specs.forEach(function (s) { %><div><dt class="mono"><%= s[0] %></dt><dd><%= s[1] %></dd></div><% }) %>
      </dl>
      <div class="cta"><a class="wsl mono" href="/workspace">Check my ESP32 code ↗</a><a class="wsl mono" href="#lab">Simulate ESP32 ↑</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="modes" data-tilt>
      <p class="mono small">CURRENT BY POWER MODE · LOG SCALE</p>
      <% esp32.modes.forEach(function (m) { %><div class="mode"><span><%= m[0] %></span><div class="b"><i style="--w:<%= (Math.log10(m[2]) / Math.log10(300000) * 100).toFixed(1) %>%"></i></div><b class="mono"><%= m[1] %></b></div><% }) %>
      <p class="tip mono"><%= esp32.tip %></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how" id="how">
    <div class="code-panel">
      <p class="mono small">FIRMWARE PHASE MARKERS</p>
<pre class="mono">EB_BEGIN("sensing");
read_sensor();
EB_END("sensing");

// Link timestamps to
// measured supply current.</pre>
      <div class="ina"><span class="mono">INA219</span></div>
      <p class="mono from">From electrons to evidence.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="how-copy">
      <h2>A clear path<br>to real hardware.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Designed around INA219 measurements and firmware phase labels. Start in the simulator, then bring your own captured data.</p>
      <div class="acc">
        <div class="item open"><button><span class="mono n">01</span>Measure the supply<i>×</i></button><p>An INA219 placed in the supply path measures bus voltage and shunt-derived current. Capture samples with timestamps on your controller or host. Sampling rate and shunt range limit which transients you can resolve.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><button><span class="mono n">02</span>Label the phase<i>+</i></button><p>Wrap each firmware phase with begin and end markers so every current sample maps to the code that caused it.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><button><span class="mono n">03</span>Verify the improvement<i>+</i></button><p>Re-measure after each change. Keep board, interval and battery assumptions identical so the comparison holds.</p></div>
        <div class="item"><button><span class="mono n">04</span>Connect the next layer<i>+</i></button><p>Feed measured traces into the same views to replace modelled phases with real ones.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="take">
    <div><p class="mono small">KNOW YOUR ENERGY BUDGET</p><h2>Take the evidence<br>with you.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Your current trace, phase breakdown and battery assumptions in one report.</p></div>
    <a class="dl" data-tilt id="report" href="/api/report"><p class="mono small">DOWNLOAD</p><h3>Energy report</h3><b>↓</b><span class="mono">.TXT / current run</span></a>
  </section>

  <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/react/18.3.1/umd/react.production.min.js"></script>
  <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/react-dom/18.3.1/umd/react-dom.production.min.js"></script>
  <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/babel-standalone/7.24.7/babel.min.js"></script>
  <script>window.BOARDS = <%- JSON.stringify(boards) %>;</script>
  <script src="/js/fx.js"></script>
  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
  <script type="text/babel" data-presets="react" src="/js/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
